      },
      account: "tailscale_join_observe_status passed tailscale_status_json_argv() (the args-only [\"status\",\"--json\"]) where the seam needs a whole argv; typed_argv_exec_over_fleet_ssh cannot tell the two shapes apart, so it dialed \"status\" as the program and the status leg exited 127 (srv4 dispatch run 44643376146). The caller is fixed to argv_words(command: tailscale_status_json_command()); the shared root remains: one List<String> carries both shapes, so any sibling caller can repeat the mistake. The two runner sites (runner_slot_actuation's ps/sleep argvs) already carry the program as word 0 and are NOT affected. Recorded, not fixed here, so the fleet join blocker stays small.",
